IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poca-nouns`
IMPORT `poca-dealing`

-- Tests for poca-dealing.l4 (sections 327, 328, 329, 334).  Every expected value is written from the text before the run.
-- Record literals are positional, in the order of the DECLARE.

§ `Facts used by the tests`

-- Disclosure and exemption facts: authorised disclosure, made before the act, appropriate consent, intended to disclose, reasonable excuse, enforcement function, adequate consideration
`no exemption facts` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an authorised disclosure after the act` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an authorised disclosure before the act without consent` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an authorised disclosure before the act with consent` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an intended disclosure with a reasonable excuse` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an intended disclosure without a reasonable excuse` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a reasonable excuse but no intention to disclose` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an enforcement function` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`adequate consideration` MEANS `Disclosure and exemption facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- Overseas conduct facts: knows or believes it occurred abroad, not unlawful there, of a prescribed description
`no overseas facts` MEANS `Overseas conduct facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`conduct lawful abroad` MEANS `Overseas conduct facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`conduct lawful abroad but of a prescribed description` MEANS `Overseas conduct facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`conduct abroad that was unlawful there` MEANS `Overseas conduct facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`conduct lawful abroad but not known to be abroad` MEANS `Overseas conduct facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Account facts: a deposit-taking body or similar, operating an account, value, threshold
`no account facts` MEANS `Account facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`an account act below the threshold` MEANS `Account facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, 2999, 3000
`an account act at the threshold` MEANS `Account facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, 3000, 3000
`an account act above the threshold` MEANS `Account facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, 3001, 3000
`an account act below a higher threshold specified under section 339A(3)` MEANS `Account facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, 4000, 5000
`an account act by a body that is not a deposit-taking body` MEANS `Account facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, 100, 3000
`an act that is not in operating an account` MEANS `Account facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, 100, 3000

-- Termination facts: carrying on business in the regulated sector, excluded business, transferring or handing over to the customer, for termination, total value, threshold, due diligence done
`no termination facts` MEANS `Termination facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`a termination transfer below the threshold` MEANS `Termination facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 2999, 3000, TRUE
`a termination transfer at the threshold` MEANS `Termination facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 3000, 3000, TRUE
`a termination transfer of excluded business` MEANS `Termination facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 2999, 3000, TRUE
`a termination transfer without due diligence` MEANS `Termination facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 2999, 3000, FALSE
`a transfer not for the termination of the relationship` MEANS `Termination facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 2999, 3000, TRUE
`a termination transfer by a business outside the regulated sector` MEANS `Termination facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 2999, 3000, TRUE
`a handing over that is not to the customer` MEANS `Termination facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 2999, 3000, TRUE

-- Mixed funds facts: regulated sector, in the course of that business for a customer, knows or suspects part is criminal, cannot identify the part, value after the act, value of the criminal part
`no mixed funds facts` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`mixed funds kept whole` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1000, 1000
`mixed funds with more kept` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 5000, 1000
`mixed funds reduced below the criminal part` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 999, 1000
`mixed funds where the criminal part can be identified` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 1000, 1000
`mixed funds where all is known to be criminal` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 1000, 1000
`mixed funds outside the regulated sector` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1000, 1000
`mixed funds not held for a customer` MEANS `Mixed funds facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 1000, 1000

§ `s 327(2) to (3) the exceptions, one at a time`
#ASSERT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `an authorised disclosure after the act`
#ASSERT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `an authorised disclosure before the act with consent`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `an authorised disclosure before the act without consent`
#ASSERT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `an intended disclosure with a reasonable excuse`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `an intended disclosure without a reasonable excuse`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `a reasonable excuse but no intention to disclose`
#ASSERT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `an enforcement function`
-- adequate consideration is a defence to section 329 only
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `adequate consideration`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` `no exemption facts`
#ASSERT `s 327(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` `conduct lawful abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` `conduct lawful abroad but of a prescribed description`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` `conduct abroad that was unlawful there`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` `conduct lawful abroad but not known to be abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` `no overseas facts`
#ASSERT `s 327(2B) the conduct is the relevant criminal conduct` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 327(2B) the conduct is the relevant criminal conduct` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2C): only the acts in paragraphs (c) and (d) of subsection (1); less than the threshold, so the threshold itself is not covered
#ASSERT `s 327(2C) the exception for acts in operating an account applies` `converts criminal property` `an account act below the threshold`
#ASSERT `s 327(2C) the exception for acts in operating an account applies` `transfers criminal property` `an account act below the threshold`
#ASSERT NOT `s 327(2C) the exception for acts in operating an account applies` `conceals criminal property` `an account act below the threshold`
