#ASSERT `s 327(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) `removes criminal property from England and Wales or from Scotland or from Northern Ireland` `no exemption facts` `no overseas facts` `no account facts` `no termination facts` `mixed funds reduced below the criminal part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 327(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) `conceals criminal property` `no exemption facts` `no overseas facts` `no account facts` `no termination facts` `mixed funds kept whole` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the regulative twin: unless the answer is JUST FALSE, the prohibition stands
#TRACE `s 327(1) the person must not conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` AT 5
#TRACE `s 327(1) the person must not conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` AT 5
#TRACE `s 327(1) the person must not conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` AT 5
#TRACE `s 327(1) the person must not conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1000

