§ `s 334 penalties`
-- offences under ss 327 to 329: six months or a fine up to the statutory maximum or both; 14 years (168 months) or a fine or both
#ASSERT (`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` `on summary conviction`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` `on summary conviction`)'s `ceiling of the fine` EQUALS `the statutory maximum`
#ASSERT (`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` `on summary conviction`)'s `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed`
#ASSERT (`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 168
#ASSERT (`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `ceiling of the fine` EQUALS `a fine with no ceiling stated`
#ASSERT (`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed`
-- offences under ss 330 to 332: six months, statutory maximum, or both; five years (60 months), a fine, or both
#ASSERT (`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` `on summary conviction`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` `on summary conviction`)'s `ceiling of the fine` EQUALS `the statutory maximum`
#ASSERT (`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` `on summary conviction`)'s `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed`
#ASSERT (`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT (`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `ceiling of the fine` EQUALS `a fine with no ceiling stated`
#ASSERT (`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed`
-- offences under s 339(1A): a fine up to level 5 on the standard scale, on summary conviction only
#ASSERT `s 334(3) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 339(1A)` `on summary conviction` EQUALS JUST (`Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 0, `ceiling of the fine` IS `level 5 on the standard scale`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 334(3) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 339(1A)` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS NOTHING
